      "text": "Let's start by understanding the problem. We have a cubic equation \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\) with roots \\(a, b, c\\). We need to find the cubic equation with roots \\(a+b, b+c, c+a\\), and then determine the constant term \\(t\\) of this new cubic equation.\n\nFirst, let's use Vieta's formulas for the original cubic equation \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\). According to Vieta's formulas:\n\\[\na + b + c = -3,\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4,\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11.\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the sum, product, and sum of the new roots \\(a+b, b+c, c+a\\). These sums are:\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a + b + c) = 2(-3) = -6,\n\\]\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) + (b+c)(c+a) + (c+a)(a+b) = ab + bc + ca + 2abc = 4 + 2 \\cdot 11 = 26,\n\\]\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a).\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\((a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\\):\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = ab + bc + ca + ab(a+c) + bc(b+a) + ca(b+c).\n\\]\n\nWe already know \\(ab + bc + ca = 4\\), so we need to calculate \\(ab(a+c) + bc(b+a) + ca(b+c)\\):\n\\[\nab(a+c) = a^2b + ac^2,\n\\]\n\\[\nbc(b+a) = b^2c + bca,\n\\]\n\\[\nca(b+c) = c^2a + abc.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = ab + bc + ca + a^2b + ac^2 + b^2c + bca + c^2a + abc = (a+b+c)(ab + bc + ca) + (abc)^2 = -3 \\cdot 4 + 11^2 = -12 + 121 = 109.\n\\]\n\nNow we have the coefficients of the new cubic equation \\(x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0\\):\n\\[\nr = -6,\n\\]\n\\[\ns = 26,\n\\]\n\\[\nt = -109.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(t\\) is \\(\\boxed{-109}\\).",
