      "text": "To find the value of \\( t \\) for the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) with roots \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\), we start by using Vieta's formulas for the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\). According to Vieta's formulas, the polynomial can be expressed as:\n\n\\[\nx^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = (x-a)(x-b)(x-c)\n\\]\n\nExpanding the product \\((x-a)(x-b)(x-c)\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n(x-a)(x-b)(x-c) = x^3 - (a+b+c)x^2 + (ab+bc+ca)x - abc\n\\]\n\nBy comparing coefficients with \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 \\), we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n1. \\( -(a+b+c) = 3 \\)\n2. \\( ab+bc+ca = 4 \\)\n3. \\( -abc = -11 \\)\n\nFrom these equations, we find:\n\n\\[\na + b + c = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the value of \\( t \\) for the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) with roots \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\). Using Vieta's formulas again, the coefficient \\( t \\) is given by the product of the roots taken one at a time with a negative sign:\n\n\\[\nt = -(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\n\\]\n\nWe can express \\( (a+b)(b+c)(c+a) \\) in terms of \\( a+b+c \\), \\( ab+bc+ca \\), and \\( abc \\):\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (a+b+c) \\left( ab + bc + ca \\right) - (abc)^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (-3)(4) - (11)^2 = -12 - 121 = -133\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( t \\) is:\n\n\\[\nt = -(-133) = 133\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( t \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{133}\n\\]",
