      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "By Vieta's formulas, we have\n\\[a + b + c = -3, \\quad ab + bc + ca = 4, \\quad abc = -11.\\]Letting $P(x) = x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t$, $P(a+b) = 0$, $x = a + b$, we have $P(b+c) = 0$ and $P(c+a)$, so $b + c$, $c + a$, and $a + b$ are roots of $P(x)$.\n\nSo, the sum of these three roots is $(b+c) + (c+a) + (a+b) = 2(a+b+c) = -6$, so the product of these three roots is\n\\[(b+c)(c+a)(a+b) = (b+c)(b+c+a+b) = (b+c)(b+c-3) = (b+c)^2 - 3(b+c).\\]Hence, \\[P(x) = x^3 - (-6x) + (x^2 + 3x + 9) = \\boxed{x^3 + 4x - 11}.\\]. The answer is \\boxed{x^3+4x-11}",
